**Notes:**

All 10 strategies passed all audit checks on real data (ADANIGREEN, RELIANCE, AXISBANK symbols):
- Array lengths correct (== len(df)) for all signal arrays
- Dtypes correct: bool for entry/exit masks, float64 for atr_arr and target_indicator
- No NaN values in any output arrays
- Signal counts are non-trivial for all strategies except 070 and 068 (rare conditions)
- is_long_only=False for all; no spurious short signals
- VWAP resets daily in strategies 065, 066, 070 (verified via .over("day_id") polars cumsum)
- ATR-based stops produce reasonable implied stop levels (below close for longs, above for shorts)
- Strategy 070 (Gap Exhaustion) fires rarely due to strict MFI < 25 condition — not a bug
- Session window enforcement is left to the backtester per CONVENTIONS.md §7

**Test data note:**
- time_minutes column must be built with Int32 (not Int8) to avoid overflow. The pipeline's
  phases.py computes `hour * 60 + minute` which returns Int8 in polars, overflowing for values
  > 127 (i.e., any time past 2:07 AM local). This audit used Int32 cast to get correct values.
  All strategy code itself is correct — it reads time_minutes and casts to np.int32, which is
  the right thing to do; the pipeline's column construction is the upstream issue.
